   - Calls `MakeExampleInputFeature001` to get the example texts.
   - Iterates over each string in the returned slice.
   - Prints the text and counts its Unicode characters using the `countUnicodeCharacters` function.

3. **`countUnicodeCharacters` Function**:
   - Converts the input string into a slice of runes (`[]rune(s)`), which correctly handles multi-byte Unicode characters.
   - Returns the length of this rune slice, effectively counting the number of Unicode characters in the text.

